learn the basic tools for studying Judaism through history, texts, communities, rituals, and material culture."}, {"id": "91e85917-f0f5-40f6-9c42-7b35dd5ae692", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jewish diversity", "children": [{"id": "1497c69b-637a-4c10-8a30-cffc359caa4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Ashkenazi"}, {"id": "9c481f7d-d223-45c2-9f1d-0a5bd7d16557", "type": "concept", "title": "Sephardi"}, {"id": "d101c46d-77e1-45e5-a443-1429479b38b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Mizrahi"}, {"id": "a2794650-437f-4d6b-b158-9fcd419e1eb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethiopian Jews"}, {"id": "24bb756e-0d56-4218-abaa-f92f096ce314", "type": "concept", "title": "Denominations"}, {"id": "2c3f532b-2a12-4438-89b1-32cb8e00356e", "type": "concept", "title": "Secular Jews"}, {"id": "540e5144-6533-4c6b-85ff-fb57918f76da", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious Zionist"}, {"id": "c0c6365a-e043-48b3-a073-96f4378e7261", "type": "concept", "title": "Haredi"}, {"id": "a57eae8b-d756-4d66-908b-eec2cd6d0feb", "type": "concept", "title": "Liberal Judaism"}], "description": "The point is to avoid treating Judaism as one uniform belief system."}, {"id": "2add1927-8bd5-4c1d-93a7-5fc0b108d195", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core source categories", "children": [{"id": "d5af5484-4894-4a05-8246-c070558a770f", "type": "concept", "title": "Tanakh"}, {"id": "54cfdd21-8603-4bf0-a1f2-06b6897acd92", "type": "concept", "title": "Torah"}, {"id": "ab162236-7020-493d-8e8c-5e40e0869910", "type": "concept", "title": "Neviim"}, {"id": "c30ac9ef-f80f-4dd0-9c31-8a9a7975761d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ketuvim"}, {"id": "c142e49b-2491-4315-a409-561ff04951f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Mishnah"}, {"id": "d899a3e6-9289-4351-8029-e6ef57c28d32", "type": "concept", "title": "Talmud"}, {"id": "8eaec960-4da0-4943-8914-cd18af46afba", "type": "concept", "title": "Midrash"}, {"id": "0c2a98d2-c704-4842-b47e-8df35bfa585a", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsa"}, {"id": "7157e937-2d81-4ddc-899b-07efa96707df", "type": "concept", "title": "Siddur"}, {"id": "afc599c5-d6d8-4ba6-b444-bc29b8eb5bf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Commentary"}], "description": "Students learn the map of Jewish textual and historical sources used throughout the course."}]}, {"id": "006a4790-02fa-44f6-b95d-e898ba1986f8", "type": "topic", "title": "Biblical and Ancient Israelite Backgrounds", "description": "Judaism's later forms draw on ancient Israelite traditions, biblical literature, covenantal language, temple practices, and prophetic critique. This unit gives students historical and textual foundations without reducing Judaism to the Bible alone.", "children": [{"id": "7e9b12d3-5354-40b1-9878-fb7e9ef7408c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ancient Israel and Judah", "children": [{"id": "acf89038-0286-4549-8772-792fd5ac228f", "type": "concept", "title": "Canaan"}, {"id": "835c0227-fc46-4ddc-b5d9-21973eb19bcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Tribes of Israel"}, {"id": "60f1938d-8770-4cce-95b1-11713000c494", "type": "concept", "title": "United monarchy"}, {"id": "ccc81797-fabd-4bce-87a3-41d4ae54e72c", "type": "concept", "title": "Kingdom of Israel"}, {"id": "66b02301-2021-4978-bf4c-5081f81a72d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Kingdom of Judah"}, {"id": "6de78647-2e11-472e-9ed4-7cd41c432104", "type": "concept", "title": "Assyrian conquest"}, {"id": "8df655f9-a3f7-4e3c-addf-7df0f08925e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Babylonian exile"}, {"id": "31692341-a36c-42bb-96b4-0e81ff411dbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Persian period"}], "description": "Students learn the historical settings behind biblical traditions and Israelite identity formation."}, {"id": "a580b48b-32a0-45c4-bf5f-23ef73eaa6c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Biblical texts and genres", "children": [{"id": "a88e0843-b7a7-4bae-847f-4fe2e81efe26", "type": "concept", "title": "Genesis"}, {"id": "84b7497c-2ec6-4c06-a260-51536b251651", "type": "concept", "title": "Exodus"}, {"id": "94b15e0f-fc3a-4a24-ab05-7023a57101c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Deuteronomy"}, {"id": "5856381f-a300-4553-ac77-81c40b124c90", "type": "concept", "title": "Prophets"}, {"id": "e6ed2662-df54-43fb-b034-6eaa85415b93", "type": "concept", "title": "Psalms"}, {"id": "eb07971a-037c-4576-84d4-24127a1abee0", "type": "concept", "title": "Proverbs"}, {"id": "0ec64e34-d5bb-465a-a549-87b7434e8c21", "type": "concept", "title": "Job"}, {"id": "977fcb59-e868-461b-ab3c-11ebd8c709a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Chronicles"}, {"id": "c9a71b32-3d92-49a7-9e37-c6711559261e", "type": "concept", "title": "Canon formation"}], "description": "The goal is to read the Hebrew Bible as a library of law, narrative, poetry, prophecy, wisdom, and memory."}, {"id": "ca90d5f6-dca0-4c24-8446-0d0b4e8899f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Covenant, law, and temple", "children": [{"id": "20ab86df-fae1-4af2-8c2b-fee843151956", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant"}, {"id": "9113afae-e1f8-448d-a6ba-5e6fe95cdbe7", "type": "concept", "title": "Mitzvot"}, {"id": "74a97fcc-c8c8-4cc4-bd69-924a108ed13f", "type": "concept", "title": "Priesthood"}, {"id": "368920ad-f05d-404e-8f51-242b277f4804", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacrifice"}, {"id": "12c73760-1914-46fe-bd58-ac5c1dcfd073", "type": "concept", "title": "Temple"}, {"id": "dd60fb9c-0d2b-476c-ae8e-555ffd7a82da", "type": "concept", "title": "Purity"}, {"id": "75b26642-17ad-4e0a-a085-4d1ec36d3cc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Sabbath"}, {"id": "bcab185d-b130-4a16-9fdf-23a98c9decc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Exile"}, {"id": "8d8fb23d-fc1a-4c49-aa07-6ae6d5d538e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Return"}], "description": "Students learn concepts that later Jewish communities reinterpret in many ways."}]}, {"id": "0f0ef2a9-d111-4359-8f13-a012371dd827", "type": "topic", "title": "Second Temple Judaism and the Emergence of Jewish Sects", "description": "The Second Temple period was a world of diversity, empire, apocalyptic hope, sectarian movements, and scriptural interpretation. Students learn how this period shaped later Judaism and early Christianity.", "children": [{"id": "5526b393-e333-428d-86fd-a0d5e22360fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical setting", "children": [{"id": "f4dc571f-2f51-49bc-af92-68ece59f0b52", "type": "concept", "title": "Second Temple"}, {"id": "a92b836e-4802-4d9e-989a-ae9ff9c6f39d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hellenism"}, {"id": "805c6ee7-6e4a-41e0-b5de-b557d0df08ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Maccabean revolt"}, {"id": "f048a9d7-8bb2-4b86-8380-c6df75267a9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hasmoneans"}, {"id": "204269b9-7847-41c0-b261-9d040c08d823", "type": "concept", "title": "Herod"}, {"id": "b666d34f-7bd5-4c77-9d90-846c7dd6773e", "type": "concept", "title": "Roman Judea"}, {"id": "e3dcb73c-fd63-4621-b852-086ea7b8dbc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora"}, {"id": "0747d43b-a091-49b9-88bb-d8a0f71f2dfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Temple economy"}], "description": "Students understand Jewish life under Persian, Hellenistic, Hasmonean, and Roman power."}, {"id": "25c7a683-314c-4d72-ae8c-3be2118c885e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jewish groups and movements", "children": [{"id": "4cbfdaa1-9f49-4b3a-89f5-36a8b865a388", "type": "concept", "title": "Pharisees"}, {"id": "34ad8dc5-03fd-47d6-96ee-edccb8e67bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Sadducees"}, {"id": "bb1c941b-b7c7-4bb3-9aac-1611bcfa1e37", "type": "concept", "title": "Essenes"}, {"id": "bc20cd0c-2933-4da8-9e35-112d98381e27", "type": "concept", "title": "Zealots"}, {"id": "2fb54ba7-2c92-4466-a6f7-60cc4be51c02", "type": "concept", "title": "Qumran"}, {"id": "2ddc2e0d-6b48-4ef3-8b27-354802c342a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Dead Sea Scrolls"}, {"id": "bc339725-28cf-4b2d-81db-f1d4a49c55db", "type": "concept", "title": "Apocalypticism"}, {"id": "5f1f7931-80fc-4265-803a-eebb6f7e41ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Scribes"}], "description": "Students learn why ancient Judaism was plural and contested."}, {"id": "558a4f54-2e10-4b0b-9ee8-f91fbf93764b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpretation and identity"