a3c41de1", "type": "concept", "title": "Baal Shem Tov"}, {"id": "350dda16-97de-4740-bcea-56914d245d1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hasidic courts"}, {"id": "b19118a6-b27c-4695-950a-9efc628fb118", "type": "concept", "title": "Rebbe"}, {"id": "a6c7a96c-ab34-4602-b467-a41854944095", "type": "concept", "title": "Devekut"}, {"id": "2eccd6a5-0359-4d21-8beb-355143cf0c6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Nigun"}, {"id": "e292806b-24de-4744-bdd9-05b855223fb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Mitnagdim"}, {"id": "d53c61ab-dcd1-4361-b074-67a6ad3da9ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Chabad"}, {"id": "78815629-3262-4d7c-b85d-067558d14015", "type": "concept", "title": "Lithuanian yeshivot"}], "description": "The point is to see modern Judaism as plural, not simply secularizing."}]}, {"id": "28947c0d-a83b-4bbd-92b3-c0458800d2df", "type": "topic", "title": "Antisemitism, Holocaust, and Jewish Memory", "description": "Modern Jewish history cannot be studied responsibly without antisemitism and the Holocaust, but Jewish history must not be reduced to persecution. This unit studies hatred, catastrophe, resistance, survival, and memory.", "children": [{"id": "5956e389-e14f-4369-a736-5de7433b51fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modern antisemitism", "children": [{"id": "be08fd18-c0e2-43ac-80e0-76147b5fb223", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-Judaism"}, {"id": "d80532c6-998c-4623-b188-f100bcddfa22", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial antisemitism"}, {"id": "be245f18-a1dc-4197-9d07-b5e48fe28375", "type": "concept", "title": "Dreyfus Affair"}, {"id": "290ef3af-d6fc-44db-a138-19c8b4197d7e", "type": "concept", "title": "Protocols of the Elders of Zion"}, {"id": "2ddbf047-e6ac-490b-ac74-6ab495d9c40c", "type": "concept", "title": "Pogroms"}, {"id": "af45a183-6863-4410-8d27-ef292188b094", "type": "concept", "title": "Scapegoating"}, {"id": "6b403991-6878-4a7d-a6a1-e3552666da9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Conspiracy theories"}, {"id": "cf9a351a-1c53-40bd-976c-32b3ca920241", "type": "concept", "title": "Antisemitism today"}], "description": "Students distinguish religious anti-Judaism from racial, political, and conspiratorial antisemitism."}, {"id": "ef9a4b78-3f5c-4a3f-a992-7c0f197aa19c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Holocaust history", "children": [{"id": "382c13d7-e776-440d-84b5-260a8dc48105", "type": "concept", "title": "Nazi ideology"}, {"id": "5e97152b-960b-47f2-aee6-b1acdbc46177", "type": "concept", "title": "Nuremberg Laws"}, {"id": "34a83703-cba4-44c4-88e9-4bc442d707b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Ghettos"}, {"id": "730061a2-16c8-4a6c-8974-d0cbfbd0bfb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Einsatzgruppen"}, {"id": "cf594e37-ea5b-4a51-be82-7a3400ca8c74", "type": "concept", "title": "Deportations"}, {"id": "b76251b8-a665-4299-b5ae-c880c7517895", "type": "concept", "title": "Camps"}, {"id": "3b074240-8e39-4d11-bb92-1f426cda33fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Final Solution"}, {"id": "4db9f228-7445-48ce-a4e7-2b7581f2d2e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Resistance"}, {"id": "bf5571e3-fa17-4ecd-baa5-4c72920192f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Survivors"}], "description": "Students learn the events, institutions, victims, perpetrators, bystanders, rescuers, and resistors of the Shoah."}, {"id": "c657e94c-8cb2-400e-af20-8c9fcd7d3568", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Memory and ethics", "children": [{"id": "21c600af-6a07-441c-9baf-1b0e00082bfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Yad Vashem"}, {"id": "fc2d5b6f-8a9c-4cca-9f09-324b248bdf9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Testimony"}, {"id": "d6f21ed6-882d-407e-8e5b-7ab008ca9ad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Memorials"}, {"id": "ff508261-c9f9-4d55-9e92-0af1cdd9b8e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Museums"}, {"id": "3863c313-bf83-41e0-bbfd-3991878692bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Yom HaShoah"}, {"id": "a9638cad-c8a3-486d-b2cb-52415f739225", "type": "concept", "title": "Postmemory"}, {"id": "cc049307-3fd2-454b-9550-79bfdbaae93d", "type": "concept", "title": "Denial"}, {"id": "3a78b402-7311-499f-8f79-2c894ca6e9f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative genocide"}, {"id": "b919ee6f-981e-49e7-acc4-125c0ce6e286", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma"}], "description": "The point is to study remembrance as historical practice, ethical obligation, and public debate."}]}, {"id": "8a9c302c-b2de-4715-9d6b-4a58d4bbbff6", "type": "topic", "title": "Zionism and Israel", "description": "Zionism and the State of Israel are central to modern Jewish history and identity, but they are also internally diverse and contested. Students learn movements, institutions, debates, and diaspora relationships.", "children": [{"id": "491f4d2e-4cc3-4bfb-9dab-37a9b4f8d141", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Zionist movements", "children": [{"id": "54618764-c101-4fb0-8fe7-05b1f52c6814", "type": "concept", "title": "Theodor Herzl"}, {"id": "748dc1e8-6170-4203-a48c-e07dbc7ea549", "type": "concept", "title": "Political Zionism"}, {"id": "e9c0e759-4709-48af-a2d4-cce206ca2293", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural Zionism"}, {"id": "7c5d1c1f-f484-4a3d-b9ee-cf62f2089892", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor Zionism"}, {"id": "537b9c90-5725-4d12-a339-b8a41b62ea29", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious Zionism"}, {"id": "e1de8f8d-a5b7-42ed-92af-75eba9eb9220", "type": "concept", "title": "Revisionist Zionism"}, {"id": "4655f22c-caa9-4707-9806-460605952ec4", "type": "concept", "title": "Aliyah"}, {"id": "452fd3b4-c7bd-4aec-950a-94486b733a5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Hebrew revival"}], "description": "Students learn the varieties of Zionism and the historical conditions that shaped them."}, {"id": "69c69a46-f273-424d-a998-810c90955412", "type": "subtopic", "title": "State formation and Israeli society", "children": [{"id": "abaa19f9-80ac-463f-a261-2166883bd8f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Yishuv"}, {"id": "15d82fa9-2042-4b1d-9d79-a22044518c5c", "type": "concept", "title": "British Mandate"}, {"id": "43a56e2e-43b9-451c-888b-76ce14665154", "type": "concept", "title": "1948 war"}, {"id": "e78e1840-c5c0-4607-8e1a-9d09fb23588